\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Effect of the minimum vortex-to-body distance on measured pressure classification at 0.99 confidence. The x-axis gives the exclusion threshold in 1 mm simulation-grid cells. Panels show the model variants. Blue, grey and orange represent fish-like, undetermined and cylinder-like fractions, respectively. Increasing exclusion of near-body vortices generally increased the fish-like fraction.}}{9}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:distance_filter}{{5}{9}{Effect of the minimum vortex-to-body distance on measured pressure classification at 0.99 confidence. The x-axis gives the exclusion threshold in 1 mm simulation-grid cells. Panels show the model variants. Blue, grey and orange represent fish-like, undetermined and cylinder-like fractions, respectively. Increasing exclusion of near-body vortices generally increased the fish-like fraction}{figure.5}{}}
\newlabel{fig:distance_filter@cref}{{[figure][5][]5}{[1][7][]9}}
